<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Boeotia</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Boiotia</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Boeotia is a region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/greece">Greece</a> north of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attica">Attica</a>, whose fertile plains were dominated in antiquity by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thebes">Thebes</a>. Its cities, including Orchomenus, Thespiae and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-plataea">Plataea</a>, formed the Boeotian League, and it was the scene of major battles such as Plataea, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-leuctra">Leuctra</a> and Chaeronea. Under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/epaminondas">Epaminondas</a>, Thebes briefly became the leading Greek power in the 360s BCE.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/boeotia.jpg" alt="Boeotia" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Voiotia_municipalities_numbered.svg: Badseed derivative work: Pitichinaccio (talk) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:2010_Dimi_Viotias_numbered.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
